From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:59:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=cmd_retire gives a ONE_TIME
 recording's holds back at its commit's completion

A ONE_TIME primary is committed once: a later submit re-records. Its
upload BOs and its command allocator hold still stayed with the command
buffer until the application reset, freed or began it again, which RDR2
does seconds or minutes later for about 1000-1660 buffers at once
(1018 MiB of upload BOs, 751 MiB of allocators nothing reset).

With MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=cmd_retire (named only, not part of "all"):

- At a ONE_TIME primary's first, direct submit, before its commit,
  kk_cmd_detach_retire moves its upload BOs, its large BOs and its
  allocator hold into a kk_cmd_retire record, and the commit's feedback
  handler is retire_commit_callback. The command buffer then owns
  nothing pending, so its later reset, free or Begin finds empty lists:
  a Vulkan fence can signal before Metal runs the handler. The handler
  never reads the command buffer.
- At completion, on a Metal thread, kk_cmd_pool_retire drops the
  allocator hold, returns the BOs to the pool's caches through the same
  code as a reset, under the pool's new retire.lock, and counts the
  pool's retirements in flight down. A pool destroy, and a pool reset
  with RELEASE_RESOURCES, wait for none to be in flight. Without the
  switch the lock is never taken.
- Allocator users are atomic. Allocators are reset, sealed and destroyed
  only on the pool's thread, at Begin (kk_cmd_pool_get_allocator), never
  at completion: a free allocator with no users is reset and taken; one
  a recording was released from without a commit is tainted and is
  destroyed instead, never reset (the IOGPU fault of resetting an
  allocator an ended, uncommitted command buffer still names); past
  8 MiB at an End it is sealed and takes no new recording until its
  reset; a pool makes new allocators up to four unsealed, then shares
  the least-filled free one.
- [kk-cmd-retire] (with MESA_KK_DEBUG=memory, after [kk-cmd-census])
  counts retirements in flight and done, and allocator resets, seals,
  taints, destroys and shares.

Reusable and simultaneous primaries, secondaries, the queue's
re-records and a failed record allocation keep today's holds. Without
the switch, allocation, release and reset are unchanged.
kk-cmd-retire-test.c checks it on the mock.

Linear: PLA-364
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-rdr2-kk-audio-diagnostics.md
Offered-upstream: no
